      "content": "The MySQL connection is persistently failing with an authentication error (`Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`) despite many retries, so I cannot execute verification queries. I have, however, gathered strong evidence from the semantic network (table/column definitions and multiple same-shape metric precedents). Below is the report, followed by the final SQL built strictly from that evidence.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (investigated via `semantic_get` / `semantic_search`):**\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — academic department dimension: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_CODE`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N'), budget code, commencement-book names. One row per department. The natural source of \"school and department combination\".\n- **SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION** — course catalog descriptions: `COURSE`, `DEPARTMENT`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` (course-level flag), `CIP_PROGRAM_CODE`, course level, effective terms. The only table carrying `CIP_PROGRAM_CODE` per course.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — catalog-level subject offerings per academic year/term: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR` ('Y'/'N'), term flags, grading, HGN. One row per subject offering per term/year.\n- **CIP / CIP_WITH_VERSION** — CIP program lookup tables (join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE); not needed since the question only requires the variance of the code itself, which lives on SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.\n- Other tables returned by search (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG, TIP_*, LIBRARY_*, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS*, facilities/HR/space tables, etc.) were screened: they either lack `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR` + school attribution in one place, or belong to unrelated domains (facilities, IAP, mailing lists).\n\n**Column concepts:**\n- **column_concept_total_units** — TOTAL_UNITS replicated across catalog/registrar tables. Its `decision_guide` explicitly says: *\"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance/geometric mean) over catalog offerings … Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\"*.\n- **column_concept_department_name** — DEPARTMENT_NAME (catalog owner) vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME (actual offering dept); SIS_DEPARTMENT/SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION/COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED all use DEPARTMENT_NAME.\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_department_dimension`, `concept_course_catalog_sources`, `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_cip_program_classification` — confirm SIS_DEPARTMENT is the degree-granting/school-attribution dimension, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the warehouse catalog offering fact, and CIP codes live on SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.\n\n**Metric precedents (full SQL retrieved):**\n- **dw_4061** — geometric mean of TOTAL_UNITS: `EXP(AVG(LN(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS)))` with `TOTAL_UNITS > 0`.\n- **dw_1033** — CIP variance: `VARIANCE(scd.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE)` from SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION with `scd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'` and Mathematics department.\n- **dw_1471 / dw_2158 / dw_3311** — \"offered this year\" = `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR = 'Y'` on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (dw_1471/dw_2158), CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (dw_3311).\n- **dw_1350** — \"for each department and school … grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, …)\" implemented as DepartmentStats `UNION ALL` SchoolRollup (`NULL AS DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME … GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME`).\n- **dw_3904 / dw_4490 / dw_1302 / dw_2850** — alternative rollup pattern using `GROUP BY … WITH ROLLUP` (with `GROUPING()`).\n- **dw_3131 / dw_2737** — \"at least N% greater/less than the overall average\" classification: `CASE WHEN v > avg * 1.2 THEN 'HIGH…' WHEN v < avg * 0.8 THEN 'LOW…' ELSE 'AVERAGE' END`, with the overall average as a CROSS JOIN scalar over per-group values (`AVG(per_group_metric)`).\n- **dw_1393** — \"degree-granting departments except the Management department\" precedent (there implemented via admin-department name; here the wording targets the department dimension directly).\n- **dw_2957** — geometric-mean-with-category precedent (`EXP(AVG(LN(...)))` + CASE category).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- `semantic_graph(query_neighbors, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION)`: joins outgoing to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE and SIS_DEPARTMENT (`DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE`); incoming from COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, CIP, CIP_WITH_VERSION, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG; member of column_concept_department_name.\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED joins SIS_DEPARTMENT via `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (documented in both tables' column definitions and used in dw_1471/dw_2158).\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED has **no** SCHOOL_NAME column (verified against its full column list) — school attribution must come from SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME, matching the phrase \"departments in that school\".\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (measure source for TOTAL_UNITS):**\n\n| Candidate | Granularity | Has IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR | School attribution | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | subject offering per term/year | YES (column list) | via SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE join | column defs; dw_1471/dw_2158 use the flag |\n| CIS_COURSE_CATALOG | catalog feed per year/term | YES (dw_3311 uses it) | via SIS_SUBJECT_CODE | dw_2272/dw_3311 |\n| DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG | alternative feed | same structure | — | concept_course_catalog_sources |\n| SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | registrar per-term facts | NO such flag (term-based instead) | own dept/school columns | column_concept_total_units comparisons |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Required measure `TOTAL_UNITS` + filter \"offered this year\": SUPPORTED by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (`IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR`, decision_guide names it for geometric mean) and CIS_COURSE_CATALOG; NOT-SUPPORTED by SUBJECT_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (no this-year flag).\n- Required filter keys `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Management'`, `SCHOOL_NAME`: exist only on SIS_DEPARTMENT (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED lacks degree-granting flag and school name) → join required.\n- Required measure `CIP_PROGRAM_CODE` + `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` (course-level) + `DEPARTMENT_NAME IS NOT NULL` + `DEPARTMENT='18'`: all exist on SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION (dw_1033 precedent).\n- Required rollup shape (dept null per school): precedents dw_1350 (UNION ALL) and dw_3904/dw_1302 (WITH ROLLUP) both SUPPORTED.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"subjects … offered this year\" → `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR = 'Y'` (dw_1471, dw_2158, dw_3311 all anchor this phrase to that column).\n- \"more than zero total units\" → `TOTAL_UNITS > 0` (dw_4061, dw_1335).\n- \"degree-granting … not the Department of Management\" (departments) → `SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' AND DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Management'` (dw_1393 anchors \"degree-granting departments except the Management department\"; dw_1350 anchors department-level IS_DEGREE_GRANTING).\n- \"degree-granting courses\" (CIP part) → course-level `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'` (dw_1033: \"degree-granting … courses\" uses `scd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`).\n- \"Mathematics department (Course 18)\" → `DEPARTMENT = '18'` (dw_1033/dw_2158 anchor Course 18 to code '18').\n- \"geometric mean\" → `EXP(AVG(LN(x)))` (dw_4061, dw_2957, dw_4701).\n- \"overall average … across all schools\" → average of the per-school geometric means (Tip #2 convention; dw_3131 computes `AVG(per-group metric)` as the overall benchmark).\n- \"at least 5% greater/less\" → `> avg*1.05` / `< avg*0.95` (dw_3131 and dw_2737 both render \"at least 20% greater/less\" as strict `>`/`<` against `avg*1.2`/`avg*0.8`).\n- \"grand total per school with department as null\" → NULL department name row per school (dw_1350 exact format match).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- Geometric mean of TOTAL_UNITS: 3 precedents, all `EXP(AVG(LN(...)))` — dw_4061 (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED), dw_4701, dw_2957.\n- \"IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR\" for \"offered this year\": dw_1471, dw_2158 (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED), dw_3311 (CIS_COURSE_CATALOG) — 2 of 3 on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, which is also the table the column_concept decision_guide names for geometric means.\n- CIP variance: dw_1033 (1 precedent, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION).\n- School rollup with null department: dw_1350 (UNION ALL), dw_3904/dw_4490/dw_1302 (WITH ROLLUP).\n- ±% classification vs overall average: dw_3131, dw_2737 (both CROSS JOIN scalar of AVG over per-group values, strict inequalities).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT is the canonical dimension for school attribution and degree-granting status (used by dw_1350, dw_1393, dw_1471, dw_1618, dw_2158).\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves catalog unit-statistics questions (dw_4061, dw_1471, dw_2158, dw_2580).\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION serves CIP/degree-granting course questions (dw_1033, dw_1618, dw_1302, dw_1427, dw_2272).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- Tables: SIS_DEPARTMENT ✔ (semantic_get, graph), SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ✔ (semantic_get, graph neighbors), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ✔ (semantic_get full columns), CIP/CIP_WITH_VERSION ✔ (search desc + graph; not needed in SQL), SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED / CIS_COURSE_CATALOG / DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED / STUDENT_DEPARTMENT / SIS_SUBJECT_CODE / ACADEMIC_TERMS(_ALL) ✔ (search descs; screened out with reasons in §3a). Facilities/HR/space/IAP/Moira tables ✔ screened out as domain-irrelevant.\n- Column concepts: column_concept_total_units ✔ (semantic_get incl. decision_guide), column_concept_department_name ✔, column_concept_subject_id / term_code / year_columns ✔ (search descs).\n- Concepts: concept_department_dimension, concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_cip_program_classification ✔ (search descs).\n- Metrics: dw_4061, dw_1033, dw_1350, dw_3904, dw_4490, dw_1302, dw_2850, dw_3131, dw_2737, dw_2957, dw_1393, dw_1471, dw_2158, dw_3311, dw_2272, dw_1618, dw_3901, dw_1427, dw_2901 ✔ (full SQL retrieved for all listed).\n- **Note:** `mysql_query` failed on every attempt with `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'` — data-level verification was impossible; all claims above cite semantic-network content only.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:**\n- Row scaffold: SIS_DEPARTMENT (`SCHOOL_NAME`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`), each combination plus a per-school rollup row with `NULL` department (dw_1350 pattern via UNION ALL — safest in MySQL, avoids WITH ROLLUP's extra (NULL,NULL) grand-total row which the question does not ask for).\n- Geometric mean: `EXP(AVG(LN(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS)))` from COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT on `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, filtered `TOTAL_UNITS > 0`, `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR='Y'`, `sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, `sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Management'`, grouped by `sd.SCHOOL_NAME` (column_concept decision_guide + dw_4061/dw_1471/dw_2158).\n- CIP variance scalar: `VARIANCE(CIP_PROGRAM_CODE)` from SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION where `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' AND DEPARTMENT_NAME IS NOT NULL AND DEPARTMENT='18'` (dw_1033).\n- Overall average scalar: `AVG()` of the per-school geometric means (Tip #2; dw_3131).\n- Category: CASE with `> overall*1.05` / `< overall*0.95` (dw_3131/dw_2737 precedent for \"at least N% greater/less\").\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** four CTEs (school-level geometric mean; overall average of school geometric means; CIP variance scalar; school+department scaffold with per-school NULL-department rollup), then LEFT JOIN scaffold→school_geo on SCHOOL_NAME, CROSS JOIN the two scalars, CASE classification, exactly 6 output columns in asked order. Caveats: schools with no qualifying subjects get NULL geometric mean and fall to 'AVERAGE' (NULL comparisons are false); no rounding applied anywhere; `VARIANCE()` is MySQL's sample-variance alias used by all precedents.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data:** COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED physically has `TOTAL_UNITS`, `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE` but no school column → SIS_DEPARTMENT join supplies `SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (verified column lists). SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION physically has `CIP_PROGRAM_CODE`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `DEPARTMENT`.\n- **Semantic network:** column_concept_total_units decision_guide names COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED for geometric means; SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION↔SIS_DEPARTMENT join edge documented; concept_department_dimension designates SIS_DEPARTMENT for degree-granting/school attribution.\n- **Business:** dw_4061 (geometric mean formula), dw_1033 (CIP variance on degree-granting Math courses), dw_1350 (null-department school rollup format), dw_3131/dw_2737 (±% ABOVE/BELOW/AVERAGE classification vs overall average of group metrics) — all same-shape precedents.\n\n**6d. Alternatives/tie-breakers:** CIS_COURSE_CATALOG also supports IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR + TOTAL_UNITS (dw_3311), but lacks the direct SIS_DEPARTMENT school/degree-granting join used by the geometric-mean precedent dw_4061 and the decision_guide; WITH ROLLUP scaffold is the alternative rollup idiom (dw_3904) but would add an unrequested (NULL,NULL) row unless filtered. DB verification was blocked by the persistent authentication failure; the query below follows the precedents exactly.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_56d8bb436f134c3e9c288db6",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH school_geo AS (\\n    SELECT sd.SCHOOL_NAME,\\n           EXP(AVG(LN(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS))) AS geometric_mean_total_units\\n    FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso\\n    JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON ccso.DEPARTMENT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE\\n    WHERE ccso.TOTAL_UNITS > 0\\n      AND ccso.IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR = 'Y'\\n      AND sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\\n      AND sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Management'\\n    GROUP BY sd.SCHOOL_NAME\\n),\\noverall_stats AS (\\n    SELECT AVG(geometric_mean_total_units) AS overall_avg_geometric_mean\\n    FROM school_geo\\n),\\ncip_stats AS (\\n    SELECT VARIANCE(CIP_PROGRAM_CODE) AS cip_program_code_variance\\n    FROM SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\\n    WHERE IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\\n      AND DEPARTMENT_NAME IS NOT NULL\\n      AND DEPARTMENT = '18'\\n),\\nschool_dept_combos AS (\\n    SELECT SCHOOL_NAME, DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n    FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT\\n    GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME, DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n    UNION ALL\\n    SELECT SCHOOL_NAME, NULL AS DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n    FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT\\n    GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME\\n)\\nSELECT c.SCHOOL_NAME,\\n       c.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n       cs.cip_program_code_variance,\\n       sg.geometric_mean_total_units,\\n       os.overall_avg_geometric_mean,\\n       CASE\\n           WHEN sg.geometric_mean_total_units > os.overall_avg_geometric_mean * 1.05 THEN 'ABOVE_AVERAGE'\\n           WHEN sg.geometric_mean_total_units < os.overall_avg_geometric_mean * 0.95 THEN 'BELOW_AVERAGE'\\n           ELSE 'AVERAGE'\\n       END AS geometric_mean_category\\nFROM school_dept_combos c\\nLEFT JOIN school_geo sg ON c.SCHOOL_NAME = sg.SCHOOL_NAME\\nCROSS JOIN overall_stats os\\nCROSS JOIN cip_stats cs\\nORDER BY c.SCHOOL_NAME, c.DEPARTMENT_NAME;\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
